>#define RND(x)	(int)(Rand() % (long)(x))
>
>Xanth :-), he told me that using the '%' operator for generation random numbers
>in a given range is not fair, as the smaller numbers have a (very small) greate
>change to be selected than the bigger numbers. This is due to the fact that
>the maximum representable integer cannot be evenly divided by the upper bound
>of the wanted range.

  
    I also believe using % here is a bad idea!  You would be surprised
    at how unrandom the random numbers can get (in many random number
    generators) using %.  The best way to fix this is:

    #define MAXLONG 2.0^32 - 1  /* for example */
    #define RND(x)	(int)(Rand() / MAXLONG * (x))

    Now you have to figure out what the maximum long integer is for each
    machine in order to be portable.  But this really is the way to get
    the most out of whatever random number generator is being used.
    
